  "bb513f5d249fe080538d0e378a3ac023908191e7350ccc8aedbef3fa8817aba2": {
    "fact_rationales": {
      "F10": "The presence of a dense infiltrate of IgG-containing plasma cells, with most being IgG4 positive, is a hallmark of IgG4-Related Disease, distinguishing it from other conditions like Sarcoidosis or Giant Cell Arteritis.",
      "F6": "Opacification of all sinuses on the right with diffuse inflammation is more typical of infectious or inflammatory conditions such as Rhinocerebral Mucormycosis or IgG4-Related Disease.",
      "F7": "Bony erosion of the medial orbital apex bone with extension of inflammation into the apex is more characteristic of aggressive conditions like Rhinocerebral Mucormycosis or IgG4-Related Disease.",
      "F8": "Elevated Serum IgG4 levels are highly suggestive of IgG4-Related Disease, which is characterized by tumor-like swelling of affected organs and elevated serum IgG4 concentrations."
    },
